  "details": "I have a collider trigger, and an Udon graph with an OnTriggerEnter method that works just fine in Editor mode. but when I go into a Test Build, I notice that the On Trigger Enter method fires as the world is loading, before I can move or do anything. This exception is thrown: \n\n`NullReferenceException: A null value was found where an object instance was required. (wrapper dynamic-method) System.Runtime.CompilerServices.ExecutionScope.lambda_method (System.Runtime.CompilerServices.ExecutionScope) <0x0009a>`\n`VRCSDK2.Udon.Udon.InvokeAll (System.Action[]) <0x0003b> (wrapper dynamic-method) System.Runtime.CompilerServices.ExecutionScope.lambda_method (System.Runtime.CompilerServices.ExecutionScope) <0x0012a>`\n`VRCSDK2.Udon.Udon.InvokeAll (System.Action[]) <0x0003b> (wrapper dynamic-method) System.Runtime.CompilerServices.ExecutionScope.lambda_method (System.Runtime.CompilerServices.ExecutionScope) <0x000ac>`\n`VRCSDK2.Udon.VRC_UdonGraph.OnTriggerEnter (UnityEngine.Collider) <0x0003a>`\n\nand then the collider trigger is broken after that, and OnTriggerEnter never fires again.\n\nRepro: Put a trigger collider on a game object with the attached node setup, and run a VRC test build",
